note 2026-11-09T13:50:00Z
    **Decision (agent, 2026-11-09):** migration reset is per record, not per definition (narrows the user's migration
    Q1 A).

    **Why:** resetting records that still decode loses data for no safety gain; audit M2 Q18, `5ccc6944`, OD54 (8).

    **Reverse:** reset every record of the definition when any is incompatible.

    **Governs:** @spec.Restore.
note 2026-11-09T13:51:00Z
    **Decision (agent, 2026-11-09):** any structural Schema change to a stored field resets the record, even a harmless
    validation change (Q19).

    **Why:** a fixed rule `flow explain --since` can list before a deploy; OD54 (9).

    **Reverse:** reset only when the old value fails to decode.

    **Governs:** @spec.Restore, @spec.Codec.
note 2026-11-09T13:52:00Z
    **Decision (agent, 2026-11-09):** the price of the rule above, said fully: an offline app loses saved drafts when
    any stored field's Schema changes, and changing a computed initial value resets too, until computed fields are
    derived on restore.

    **Why:** the cost of an automatic reset without migration functions.

    **Reverse:** a decode-based reset.

    **Governs:** @spec.Restore.
note 2026-11-09T13:53:00Z
    **Decision (agent, 2026-11-09):** a dropped field is applied at that release's boot, rewriting the records holding
    it (Q20), a bounded exception to D111.

    **Why:** a later re-add starts empty instead of resurrecting old data; OD54 (10).

    **Reverse:** keep D111 strict and accept resurrection.

    **Governs:** @spec.Restore.
note 2026-11-09T13:54:00Z
    **Decision (agent, 2026-11-09):** a new identity gets its own lane (Q17); the old identity's in-flight write is
    kept, blocks nothing, is reported at every boot, and ends only by its own answer; `forget` does not release it.

    **Why:** a lane is (identity, contract, key); OD54 (7).

    **Reverse:** needs a new word (an identity route), the user's API call.

    **Governs:** @spec.WriteLanes, @spec.Restore.
note 2026-11-09T13:55:00Z
    **Decision (agent, 2026-11-09):** the repair bound resets at `RepairOverdue`: 3 asks, then `RepairOverdue`, then the
    count starts again.

    **Why:** a doubt on a long-open screen is never stranded; stage A close-out B1, `d3d89576`.

    **Reverse:** one rule.

    **Governs:** @plan.EntityDomains.
note 2026-11-09T13:56:00Z
